{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.a4_leadingTerm_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.a4_leadingTerm_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L171-L179","doc":"**A=4 leading term is nonpositive.** Instantiating the above at the derived\nA=4 witnessed data (`c = −96 < 0`, witnessed order `6`, even): the leading term of `1 − τ₄` in `(q−1)`\nis nonpositive for every `q`. With the nonvanishing leading coefficient this is\nthe derived statement behind `τ_L₄ > 1` near `q = 1` — replacing the measured\nantecedent of `MilnorParitySignLaw.sign_law_A4_measured`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.pow_six_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.pow_six_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L164-L169","doc":"The A=4 leading power `x⁶` is nonnegative (it is `(x³)²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingTerm_nonpos_of_neg_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingTerm_nonpos_of_neg_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L154-L162","doc":"**Sign is carried by the leading coefficient.** Over a linear ordered ring,\nif the leading coefficient is negative and the leading power is nonnegative (which\nan even order guarantees), the leading term `c · xⁿ` is nonpositive for every `x`\n— the structural reason the A=4 deficit `1 − τ₄` is negative near `q = 1`\n(`x = q − 1`), independently of the pin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingOrder_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingOrder_even","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L149-L152","doc":"The law's order is even at **every** `A` — a genuine `∀`-statement about the\nformula (not a data check), so it also covers the un-computed `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedOrder_even_at_known_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedOrder_even_at_known_A","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L141-L147","doc":"**The witnessed orders are even.** Needed because it is what makes the\ndeficit's sign near `q = 1` be carried entirely by the leading coefficient\n(`(q−1)^even ≥ 0`). Stated on the *witnessed* orders, so it is a fact about the\ncomputation's output, not about the formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.law_matches_witnessed_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.law_matches_witnessed_sign","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L131-L139","doc":"**The law reproduces the witnessed signs.** At both computed `A`, the sign of\nthe witnessed leading coefficient equals the independently-defined parity sign\n`(−1)^(A−1)`. Falsifiable: a *positive* witnessed A=4 coefficient would break it.\nAt A=3 this recovers the corpus's proved Borromean positivity; at A=4 it is the\nnew content — previously the sign entered only as a measured `τ_L₄ > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.law_reproduces_witnessed_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.law_reproduces_witnessed_order","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L122-L129","doc":"**The law reproduces the witnessed orders.** At both computed `A`, the\nindependently-defined formula `2(A−1)` equals the order the symbolic derivation\nactually returned. This is falsifiable: a witnessed order of `5` at `A = 4`\nwould break it. (At A=4 the witnessed value is the *exact* valuation `6`,\nreplacing the earlier log-log slope estimate `≈ 6.06`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.paritySign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.paritySign","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L116-L118","doc":"**THE LAW.** The parity sign `(−1)^(A−1)`: odd `A ↦ +1`, even `A ↦ −1`,\ndefined independently of the data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.leadingOrder","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L112-L114","doc":"**THE LAW.** The Milnor order law `2(A−1)`, defined independently of the\ndata. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedLeadingCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedLeadingCoeff","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L105-L110","doc":"**DATA (witness transcription).** Leading `(q−1)`-coefficient of `1 − τ_A`\nfrom the same witness (A=3 `+12`, A=4 `−96`). Asserts nothing on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.witnessedOrder","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BrunnianDeficitLeadingOrderDerived.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**DATA (witness transcription).** Leading `(q−1)`-order of `1 − τ_A` as\nproduced by the exact symbolic derivation, per\n`a4-brunnian-deficit-closed-form.witness.json`. `0` marks \"not computed\" — the\nlaw has exactly two data points. Asserts nothing on its own. ","signatureChunk":0}]}